<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n107592" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπερικταίνοντο</span></b> ,
			3pl.
		impf.
		
			Pass.
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hobbled along
				beneath,</i> in the phrase 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γούνατα δ᾽ ἐρρώσαντο, πόδες δ᾽
					ὑπερικταίνοντο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.3
				</span></i>
			: according to <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> it meant <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγαν ἐπάλλοντο,</span>
			and other ancient critics gave other explanations, v.
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				779.9
			</span></i>; a reading <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποακταίνοντο </span>( 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔτρεμον</span>
			) is mentioned in <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκταίνω.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
